FAQ
Frequently asked questions

Everything you need to know before starting to supply us. Can't find your answer? Reach out directly.

What is the minimum order quantity?
For first-time suppliers, we accept lots from 50 units upwards to build trust. For ongoing relationships, we prefer full container loads (typically 5,000–10,000+ units depending on model mix). Smaller lots can be consolidated with other suppliers.
How quickly do I get paid?
Payment terms depend on our relationship and the shipment size. New suppliers typically receive payment against documents (CAD) or via escrow. Established partners can access 30–60 day credit terms. We always confirm payment terms in writing before shipment.
Do you buy locked or iCloud-locked phones?
We accept carrier-locked phones (they can be unlocked or sold in specific markets). iCloud-locked (activation locked) devices are accepted only as Grade F / parts units at reduced pricing. We do not accept stolen or blacklisted IMEI devices — all lots are checked against IMEI databases.
What if my shipment doesn't match the agreed grade?
We reconcile every shipment on arrival. If devices are graded lower than agreed, we document each unit with photos and offer two options: (1) accept the lower grade at adjusted pricing, or (2) return the mismatched units at our cost for verified discrepancies. We believe in fair resolution, not unilateral deductions.
Do you handle shipping and customs?
Yes. Depending on the agreed trade term (FOB/CIF/EXW/DAP), we can coordinate freight forwarding, insurance, and Hong Kong import clearance. Our logistics team handles all documentation so you don't have to navigate customs procedures.
How do I get started?
Simply send us your stock list via the contact form or email. Include brand, model, quantity, grade, and any known issues. We'll respond within 24 hours with a quote. If we agree on pricing, we arrange samples or inspection, then schedule your first shipment.
